Message-ID: <PACS-L%93061710280743@UHUPVM1.UH.EDU>
Newsgroups: bit.listserv.pacs-l
Date:         Thu, 17 Jun 1993 10:26:53 CDT
From:         Public-Access Computer Systems Forum <LIBPACS@UHUPVM1.BITNET>
Subject:       Internet Federal Register Update, Pt.1/2

From: Rob Raisch <raisch@ora.com>
Subject: Internet Federal Register Update, Pt. 1/2

The recent signing of the GPO Access Bill ("Government Printing
Office Electronic Information Access Enhancement Act of 1993"),
Pub. L. No. 103-40, 107 State. 112 (1993) [codified at 44 U.S.C.
4101-4104 (1993)] by President Clinton may help to boost the
Internet as the delivery system of choice for GPO data.  The GPO
Access Bill mandates that the GPO provide federal data to the
public in electronic form.  Based on our brief history of serving
the daily Federal Register on the Internet we are convinced that
the Internet fits the requirements of the Access bill today.
To support this claim  we have compiled some usage statistics for
the Internet Federal Register.

Please note that the Internet Federal Register service has not
been advertised or promoted in any significant way and the usage
level, in our opinion, is indicative of the value of the
information and the power of the Internet.

Counterpoint has been serving the daily Federal Register on the
Internet for about five months.  The Register is available via
telnet, Gopher, WAIS and NNTP.  Access to the Gopher server is
free of charge with limitations on the amount of information you
can retrieve.  Using any Gopher client program, connect to
'gopher.netsys.com' on port 2001.

Please direct inquiries to 'fedreg@internet.com'

------------------------------------------------------------

Total Number of Connecting Users:  52150

                         in 32 countries on 6 continents.

Including Users from:

                         296 Educational Institutions
                         82  Commercial Entities
                         29  Government Agencies

There were 1707 hosts connecting which provided the information
required to track their host name. 538 hosts connected who did
not supply a host or domain name.

Total Number of Contacting Hosts: 2245

